# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit the real .env.
BASE_URL=https://dev.reporty.sa
LOGIN_EMAIL=your-test-account@example.com
LOGIN_PASSWORD=changeme

# Sandbox WhatsApp destination number for any real-send test (sendReply,
# template test-send). NEVER point this at a real patient number.
TEST_WA_NUMBER=+6281266850960

# --- Maha "AI Instructions" suite (scenarios/maha-instructions/) ---
# Optional: skip the wizard-step-3 confirmation prompt phrase used by the
# runbook. Defaults to "نعم" per what was observed in real prod chat logs.
CONFIRM_PHRASE=نعم
# Real per-clinic values needed for some Section A/B tests to run
# meaningfully (they skip, or don't revert to baseline, without these).
TEST_DOCTOR_NAME=
TEST_CLINIC_NAME_ORIGINAL=
TEST_INSTAGRAM_ORIGINAL=
# Set to 1 to allow the (dangerous) reset-to-baseline test in Section B.
# Leave unset/0 unless you specifically mean to run it.
ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE_RESET=0

# --- ETM suite (07-expected-text-mismatch.spec.ts) ---
# How many un-confirmed re-draft turns to send before confirming. The bug needs
# the model to build a stale draft of its own first, so <2 makes the test
# meaningless (it self-reports NEEDS_REVIEW + skips in that case). Raise it if a
# run reports "drift premise did not hold"; each extra round costs one real
# Maha round trip (~20-45s).
ETM_DRIFT_ROUNDS=3
# Upper bound for that loop. ETM_DRIFT_ROUNDS is a FLOOR: the drift phase keeps
# nudging until it has seen 2 materially different drafts (a real supersede),
# because whether Maha re-drafts or just re-explains the pending proposal is
# stochastic. A run that never gets a supersede reports UNABLE_TO_TEST rather
# than a meaningless pass — raise this if you see that often.
ETM_MAX_DRIFT_ROUNDS=6

# --- OB4/Phase4 suite (scenarios/ob4-crm-export/) — LOCAL ONLY, see below ---
# Covers QA_TestScript_Phase4_CRM_Export.md (reporty-web-backup repo root),
# Phase 1 only (Part 3, Part 3b, CRM-08 STUB, CRM-01..12, EXP-01..08,
# RMD-01..04, DSP-01) — see README.md for what Phase 1 covers and why the
# rest (Phase 2, TPL-01/02, UAP-01..04) is deliberately not scripted yet.
#
# This suite REFUSES to run unless BASE_URL is a local host (helpers/ob4-
# local-guard.ts throws otherwise) — several test cases need to edit
# config.json and restart reporty-onboard-phase3, which must never happen
# against the shared dev server. Required local setup (see the
# reference-onboard-phase3-local-integration-setup memory for the full
# writeup and known gotchas):
#   1. reporty-web-backup: `php artisan serve --port=8000`
#   2. reporty-onboard-phase3: `.venv/bin/python app.py` (listens on 9559;
#      reporty-web-backup's own .env needs ONBOARDING_SERVICE_URL=
#      http://localhost:9559 — the config/services.php fallback is a
#      different, wrong port)
#   Both point at the same real dev DB — only the app/service layer is
#   local, not the data.
# The npm run test:ob4-*/login-setup:local* scripts already set
# BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000 for you; only override the BASE_URL line
# above if your local Laravel runs on a different port.
#
# Primary OB4 SA identity (2026-09-07) — a real multi-branch clinic (2
# branches, 88 real patients), replacing the old clinic-440 default. Fill in
# and run `npm run login-setup:local-ob4sa` to produce
# auth/.storage-state.ob4sa.local.json (used by every OB4 spec file except
# the BA/BA2/orphan/single-branch ones below).
LOGIN_EMAIL_OB4SA=
LOGIN_PASSWORD_OB4SA=

# Dedicated single-branch SA — used ONLY by TC-P3-01, which specifically
# needs a genuinely single-branch clinic (the primary OB4SA account above is
# multi-branch on purpose, for the branch-isolation tests). Run
# `npm run login-setup:local-singlebranch` to produce
# auth/.storage-state.singlebranch.local.json.
LOGIN_EMAIL_SINGLEBRANCH=
LOGIN_PASSWORD_SINGLEBRANCH=

# Real branch_admin (BA) test account — users.role_id=2, parent_user_id =
# LOGIN_EMAIL_OB4SA's clinic id, pinned to one specific branch (branch_id set
# on user_infos). Needed for TC-P3-02 (role resolves to branch_admin, not
# super_admin) and every branch-scope negative check across CRM/EXP/RMD.
# Fill these in and run `npm run login-setup:local-ba` to produce
# auth/.storage-state.ba.local.json.
LOGIN_EMAIL_BA=
LOGIN_PASSWORD_BA=

# Second real branch_admin, SAME clinic as LOGIN_EMAIL_BA but pinned to a
# DIFFERENT branch — makes branch-isolation checks genuinely testable (not
# just "no branch set, defaults to branch 1 either way"). Also serves as the
# "unauthorized third party" in TC-RMD03-03's security-gap check. Run
# `npm run login-setup:local-ba2` to produce auth/.storage-state.ba2.local.json.
LOGIN_EMAIL_BA2=
LOGIN_PASSWORD_BA2=

# Deliberately malformed "orphaned staff" test account — users.role_id=2 but
# parent_user_id does NOT match any valid clinic owner. Needed for TC-P3-04
# (privilege-escalation fail-safe: must degrade to `doctor`, never rise to
# `super_admin`). There's no safe way for this suite to create this row
# itself — set it up manually in the dev DB per the test script's TC-P3-04
# precondition, then run `npm run login-setup:local-orphan`.
LOGIN_EMAIL_ORPHAN=
LOGIN_PASSWORD_ORPHAN=
# Set to 1 only after manually enabling `"phase4Capabilities": {"crm": "*"}`
# (or the specific test clinic id) in your LOCAL reporty-onboard-phase3
# config.json and restarting app.py, to run TC-CRM08-STUB-01 (positive
# stub-honesty check). Leave 0/unset otherwise — with the capability off
# (today's default), that test is meaningless and TC-CRM08-STUB-02 (the
# negative/default-off check) already covers the default state. This same
# gate now also covers the rest of the CRM-01..12 tool surface (Phase 1,
# scenarios/ob4-crm-export/06-15.spec.ts) — they all live under the same
# config.json "crm" capability group.
TEST_CRM_CAPABILITY_ENABLED=0

# Same idea as TEST_CRM_CAPABILITY_ENABLED, but for the "export" capability
# group (EXP-01..08 tools, scenarios/ob4-crm-export/16-23.spec.ts). Every
# export tool works off a set_ref produced by crm_search_contacts, so these
# tests also need TEST_CRM_CAPABILITY_ENABLED=1.
TEST_EXPORT_CAPABILITY_ENABLED=0

# Same idea, for the "staff_reminders" capability group (RMD-01..04 tools,
# scenarios/ob4-crm-export/24-27.spec.ts).
TEST_STAFF_REMINDERS_CAPABILITY_ENABLED=0

# Same idea, for the "charts" capability group (DSP-01 render_chart,
# scenarios/ob4-crm-export/28-dsp01-render-chart.spec.ts).
TEST_CHARTS_CAPABILITY_ENABLED=0

# --- Phase 1 CRM/EXP/RMD/DSP real-tool tests (scenarios/ob4-crm-export/05-28) ---
# These tools resolve contacts/staff/branches by numeric id only — there is no
# name-to-id resolution tool (same gap 05-crm05-add-note.spec.ts documented for
# crm_search_contacts). Leave any of these unset and the test(s) that need it
# skip cleanly with a clear reason, rather than guessing at an id that might not
# exist or might belong to someone else's real data.

# The primary/default real contact_id under LOGIN_EMAIL_OB4SA's clinic — used
# by most positive CRM/EXP tests (CRM-02/05/etc.) as "the" test contact.
TEST_CONTACT_ID=

# A second real contact_id in a DIFFERENT branch than TEST_CRM_CAPABILITY_ENABLED's
# clinic's default/BA branch — needed for TC-CRM02-03 (cross-branch access must
# be rejected/not leak).
TEST_CONTACT_ID_OTHER_BRANCH=

# Any second real contact_id with its own distinct phone number — needed for
# TC-CRM03-04 (duplicate-phone update must be rejected, not silently applied).
TEST_CONTACT_ID_SECONDARY=

# A real staff member's numeric users.id and display name, in the same clinic as
# TEST_CRM_CAPABILITY_ENABLED's test clinic — the "assignee" for TC-CRM04-01
# (crm_set_responsible) and TC-CRM06-01/03/04 (follow-up assignee).
TEST_CRM_ASSIGNEE_ID=
TEST_CRM_ASSIGNEE_NAME=

# TC-CRM04-04 (BA branch-scope negative for crm_set_responsible): a contact in
# the BA's own branch, and a staff member's id+name OUTSIDE the BA's branch (the
# assignment must be rejected).
TEST_CRM04_BRANCH_CONTACT_ID=
TEST_CRM04_OUT_OF_BRANCH_ASSIGNEE_ID=
TEST_CRM04_OUT_OF_BRANCH_ASSIGNEE_NAME=

# TC-CRM07-01..04 (crm_merge_contacts): a real pair of contact_ids that are
# genuine duplicates of the same person (e.g. same person entered twice) —
# create one manually per the test script's own TC-CRM07 setup steps if you
# don't already have one, since merging is destructive and shouldn't run
# against an arbitrary pair.
TEST_CRM07_DUPLICATE_CONTACT_ID_A=
TEST_CRM07_DUPLICATE_CONTACT_ID_B=

# TC-CRM02-06 (ambiguous_duplicate_phone branch-scope leak, found+fixed
# 2026-09-11): two real contact_ids under LOGIN_EMAIL_OB4SA's clinic that
# deliberately share the SAME phone_number (same failure shape as the
# patients:backfill duplicate-contact bug, still open as of this writing) —
# create one manually (insert a second patients row with an existing contact's
# exact phone_number, e.g. via a raw INSERT — there is no crm_create_contact
# tool) and make sure AT LEAST ONE of the two is linked to branch_id=1 via
# user_patient_phone_branch, so the test can prove neither one leaks access
# through the other's link.
TEST_CRM02_DUPLICATE_PHONE_CONTACT_ID_A=
TEST_CRM02_DUPLICATE_PHONE_CONTACT_ID_B=

# TC-RMD01-04 (staff_reminder_create branch-scope negative), TC-RMD02-02/03,
# TC-RMD03-01/02/03 (staff_reminder_cancel creator/target/unauthorized-third-
# party checks): the real numeric users.id backing LOGIN_EMAIL_BA — these
# reminder tools take a numeric target_id only, no name resolution.
TEST_BA_USER_ID=

# TC-RMD01-04: a real staff member's numeric users.id OUTSIDE the BA's own
# branch scope (the reminder target must be rejected).
TEST_STAFF_OUT_OF_SCOPE_ID=

# TC-RMD03-03 (⚠️ security-gap verification — see 26-rmd03-cancel-reminder.spec.ts's
# header comment) reuses LOGIN_EMAIL_BA2 above as the "unauthorized third party" —
# no separate account needed now that BA/BA2 are both real staff of the same clinic.

# --- TPL-01/02 template_studio (scenarios/ob4-crm-export/30-31.spec.ts, added 2026-09-14) ---
# Same idea as the other TEST_*_CAPABILITY_ENABLED gates, for the "template_studio"
# capability group (create_template/stage_template_send/get_template_status).
# Already wildcarded ("*", all clinics) in this checkout's local
# reporty-onboard-phase3/config.json as of 2026-09-14 — see inapp_agent/core/
# capabilities.py for the exact key.
#
# ⚠️ These tools proxy to Laravel's new AgentTemplateController (commit 1608a87c9),
# gated behind reporty-web-backup's own AGENT_EXPORT_SECRET env var — confirmed
# MISSING from that repo's .env as of this writing (only present in
# reporty-onboard-phase3's config.json and in a stray, un-loaded ".env copy" file
# over there). Every agent/templates/* call 403s with {"error":"unauthorized"}
# until reporty-web-backup/.env gets AGENT_EXPORT_SECRET set to match config.json's
# agentExportSecret — that fix is outside THIS repo's scope. See
# 30-tpl01-create-template.spec.ts's header for exactly how the tests degrade
# (self-detecting, not silently skipped) while this is unset.
TEST_TEMPLATE_STUDIO_CAPABILITY_ENABLED=0

# A real segment under LOGIN_EMAIL_OB4SA's clinic with keep_updating=OFF (frozen)
# and its known frozen-member count — proves TPL-02's frozen-segment fix
# (stage_template_send must use the FROZEN segment_frozen_members snapshot, not
# re-resolve live criteria). crm_save_as_segment (CRM-12, the only segment-creating
# tool this suite's own chat surface exposes) always creates keep_updating=True —
# there is no way to mint a frozen segment from this suite's own chat flow, so this
# reuses a real, pre-existing fixture instead (clinic 611's "QA_SEND_TEST_2NUM",
# referenced in template_studio.py's own docstring).
TEST_FROZEN_SEGMENT_ID=
TEST_FROZEN_SEGMENT_EXPECTED_COUNT=

# A real, existing (any status) template_id under this clinic, needed to get PAST
# stage_template_send's checkApproved() lookup to a real audience_count — this
# suite has no safe way to mint one itself (see 30-tpl01-create-template.spec.ts's
# header: real template creation hits the live Meta Graph API for real). Leave
# unset and the frozen-segment test still runs, but may report template_not_found
# instead of a real audience_count once/if the AGENT_EXPORT_SECRET gap above is
# fixed.
TEST_APPROVED_TEMPLATE_ID=
